# Review notes: open questions, observations and improvements

Notes from reviewing the KS2 SATs score model against the brief and the data. Some items repeat
README §4 and §6 or the review session in `docs/ai/prompts.md`; items marked **(new)** appear here
for the first time. Nothing in this file has been applied to the code yet.

---

## 1. Questions about the data

These need an answer from the product or engineering team, not a modelling decision.

| # | Question | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Why do the same (session, question) pairs appear 2–5 times with identical timestamps but different `is_correct`? | 850 conflicting questions in official subjects. The tie rule moves scores by up to 4 points. Looks like a client retry or logging bug. |
| 2 | Why does `responses.session_type` always say `MOCK_TEST` when the sitting says `summative_assessment`? | Currently ignored. If it is a hard-coded default, it should be fixed or dropped at source. |
| 3 | What are the 56 sessions with responses but no sitting record? | 1,146 official-subject questions are excluded. If these are real assessments, pupils lose evidence. |
| 4 | What does `is_correct` mean on Wellbeing survey answers (about 61% true)? | Possibly a "positive answer" code. It must never be read as attainment. |
| 5 | Are Screeners timed? Their no-attempt rate is 11.8%, about three times other subjects. | If unreached questions count as wrong, Screener scores are biased down. |
| 6 | Are assessments pitched at the pupil's year group? | The whole model assumes "53% on a Year 3 test" means "on track for 100". Average percent correct is flat across Years 1–6, which supports it, but it is not confirmed. |
| 7 | Why do 6 pupils have two different year groups in one academic year (e.g. Year 1 and Year 3)? | Could be data entry, a school move, or an assessment assigned to the wrong year. |
| 8 | Science has questions in the hierarchy but no responses. Is that expected? | Every pupil gets `no_evidence` for Science today. |
| 9 | Can the hierarchy expose topic names? | Without them English Reading and GPS can't be separated, so English uses an averaged curve. |
| 10 | Can raw tables get `created_at` / `updated_at` / ingestion timestamps? | Needed for true "what did the dashboard show on date X" and for detecting changed or deleted sittings incrementally. |
| 11 | How are deleted pupils handled downstream (e.g. GDPR erasure)? **(new)** | They are hidden in the as-of function, but their rows remain in the history table. |
| 12 | Does `pupils` have a join or creation date? **(new)** | Without it, a pupil appears in as-of results for dates before they joined. |

