## 5. Questions about the brief

- **"Every subject".** Read first as every SATs subject, then revised to every Atom subject with a
  `mapping_type` (official / proxy / not_attainment). Worth confirming which reading the product team
  intended.
- **Who sees proxy scores?** Teachers may read any 80–120 number as a SATs result. Decide whether the
  app shows proxy scores, labels them, or hides them.
- **How fresh must scores be?** Daily batch is assumed. Near real-time after each sitting would change
  the incremental design.
- **Which point in time matters?** "Score as it truly was at T" (built) or "score the teacher saw at T"
  (needs ingestion timestamps).

---

## 6. Suggested order of work

1. Fix the 196-day claim and the profiling query.
2. Add the curve-anchor and sitting-coverage tests.
3. Switch to the latest 5 sittings and rebuild.
4. Set `meets_expected_standard` to NULL for proxy subjects.
5. Raise questions 1, 3, 5 and 10 from §1 with engineering.
6. Partition raw `responses` and make de-duplication incremental.
7. Agree with product how proxy scores and younger pupils' scores are shown.
8. Start calibration once real KS2 results are available from partner schools.
